the Las Vegas Senior Softball  Association hitting a home run for many  of its players looking to stay in shape  and also create some friendships Mary  Jane beliesa shares how the love for the  game keeps military veterans connected  out on the field you can feel the  competitiveness of the game  but you can sense the teamwork too  the Las Vegas senior Association plays  softball every week at Lorenzi Park it's  a bond that grew over time not just with  the players but also for the military  veterans looking for an outlet to stay  in shape and connect with the community  Russ Curtis is the field commissioner  for the team he served in the U.S Air  Force from 1965 to 1969. they enjoy it  and a lot of them are pretty Rusty when  they first come out they don't realize  that we're as good as we are you know we  might be you know we we range from 50  years old to 80 years old on this field  Paul Callahan attended the Merchant  Marine Academy and commissioned as an  Ensign in the Navy Callahan says it's  more than just playing a game and the  camaraderie is clear to see these are  our brothers or friends some of us have  lost our spouses we rely on each other  okay I've been on the same travel team  since 2005 and we're real close-knit  knit group and it just means everything  U.S army veteran Mike razorka served two  tours in Vietnam he says the team is  always looking for more players and you  don't have to be a veteran to join I  made a few phone calls and I found out  that they play senior ball here and  being retired I was available so I  found out about this came down and was  immediately put on a on the roster and  I've been playing now for almost nine  years it's not just the guys getting in  all the fun in action but women are too  Rhonda Decker served almost 30 years in  the U.S army she says there are 61  players in the women's league with the  same goal of promoting Health as well as  quality of life and building lifelong  connections win or lose we're all you  know shaking hands in fact we're all  friends and and you know oftentimes  move teams so uh you know it's just  great way to get out like I said get  some exercise  the Las Vegas Senior Softball  Association is open to those 50 years  and older with the oldest player  currently on the league listen to this  87 years old
 

